timental attachment to  broken things but it's also someone who  longs to escape their circumstances the  bridge symbolizing a means to get away  something Vic does several times  throughout the episode this bridge also  tells us we're looking for someone who  likes to  traverse geographical locations who  perhaps longs to escape their  circumstances but using one's enscape  comes at a price for Vick it takes a  physical toll she experiences headaches  nausea and bloody eyes so using it as  many times as she wants is out of the  question another unique aspect of in  escapes is that they can be used to  transport others not just the strong  creative who conjures them for example  Joe brings Vic into the dark tunnels and  Charlie brings the children to Christmas  land but in escapes require one key  component in order to work what Maggie  calls a knife because knives cut the  fabric between the real world and the  world of thought they are the devices  which allow you access to your inscape  and escape itself world dreams up in  your imagination everybody has them but  only strong creatives can pull theirs  into the real world with the help of a  knife for Vic  it's a motorbike for Joe it's her roller  skates and for Charlie it's his  rolls-royce dubbed the Wraith without  ones knife you can't access your enscape  which is why when Charlie throws her  motorcycle into her inscape she believes  it to be gone for good how can she get  into her enscape when the thing that  allows her to access it is gone but if  there's one thing we've learned from  Jolene is that knives can manifest  themselves in different ways to  accommodate the physical limits of their  creative I didn't know you could have  more than one I thought my dirtbike was  it I thought to say when Joe was young  her knife were her roller skates but as  she grew old she couldn't muster the  speed to travel any more but one day a  new knife came to her a wheelchair  before she too couldn't handle that it's  only until Vic comes along that she's  able to push her wheelchair fast enough  in order to access her inscape Jolene's  ability is also different from Vic's  Jolene is able to essentially spy on  anyone of course when they spy on  Charlie he notices it he can sense the  power of strong creatives  actually  it's in this scene that Vik learns  Charlie's power is linked to the Wraith  when Jolene overheats the engine Charlie  melts from his younger form into an old  man we see this happen in the final  episode when Vic uses gas to burn the  Wraith and Charlie's physical form melts  along with it but burning the Wraith had  its consequences in the backseat was  Vic's lover Craig who she couldn't save  due to this barrier which only Charlie  could bring people in and out of it was  the price Vic had to pay in order to  stop Charlie but as will later find out  the car was not fully destroyed in the  last scene of the season we see a  mechanic starting to work on the burnt  to a crisp rolls-royce as he jumped  starts the car so too does Charlie  scaring the daylights out of a nurse who  was prepping him for a blood transfusion  and it's fitting that one of the final  shots is of this blood since the show's  name is not only allusion to Charlie's  license plate but also the vampire  Nosferatu also a being which could live  forever one of the more shocking  revelations was Vic's pregnancy and for  a girl who wants nothing more than to  leave Haverhill this puts a huge wrench  in things Vic starts off the season  wanting nothing more than to attend RISD  the Rhode Island School of Design she's  not shy in expressing her thoughts about  Haverhill either for Victor's two  options leave town or stay and get  knocked up and start a family she's seen  what the latter option has done to her  parents her dad is an abusive alcoholic  and her mom doesn't support her decision  to leave if her mom had it her way she'd  worked the rest of her life cleaning  homes making an honest wage rather than  trekking out to the city to be a  starving artist her dad on the other  hand believes in her but also happens to  be an alcoholic who has to ice his hands  from smacking around mom so much he  knocked her up when he was young and had  to put his music career aside something  I'm sure he resents her for I thought  that I was gonna go to like a real music  school service expensive  I need to get a job couldn't do it  regardless Vic is the most important  thing in his life and over the course of  the season we see him fail at being a  father countless times but in the end he  makes his biggest sacrifice  by giving up drinking in order to get  closer with his daughter Vic also goes  through the change of being the  reluctant hero when she's first  approached by Maggie she pleads to her  you are the only person that can stop  him ok the girl finds lost things can  find lost children don't you see you've  been chosen but Vic doesn't want this  responsibility it's only until Hayley's  kidnapping and the death of Hayley's  mother that Vic realizes Charley must be  stopped for good and her powers are the  only ones that can stop it Vic is able  to find lost things using her enscape  like her father's watch Craig's  childhood bunny and even people if she  could somehow harness her power to find  Christmas land perhaps she could find  the children and that's a huge question  mark for the season with Charlie taken  care of where are the kids  and is there even a Christmas land  anymore Maggie tells Vic that she  consulted the Scrabble pieces and for  the first time at least that we know of  they come out blank but it's safe to say  that this isn't the last we've heard of  Christmas land especially with this  season 2 on the way in the books the  story fast for it's 12 years from the  events of the gas station where Vic is  constantly haunted by the voices of the  vampire children they're pissed at what  she's done to their father Charlie we  get a hint of this when Vic is seen  outside Charlie's burned down house also  visibly pregnant my best guess for next  season is that the show will follow a  similar time jump one in which Charlie  has recovered and Vic is now raising a  young child we know that Charlie  collects children from parents who he  has deemed naughty and with him seeing  Vic as impure after he found out she  slept with Craig it's pretty much  guaranteed he's going to come after her  child but what of the other children at  Christmas land can they be saved  according to the books yes in fact they  later find out that by smashing the  ornaments you can return a vampire child  back to its human form but there was an  alternate ending in which some of the  ornaments survived and the vampires  somehow make it into the real world so  if this is a show that goes beyond two  seasons it will have to expand outside  of Christmas land and Haverhill there's  also the question of being who is one of  my favorite characters  the show beings goal in life was to get  to Christmas land where there's nothing  but joy and happiness something here on  eclis found in a comic Vic gave him  being is so taken aback by Christmas  land he writes a letter to the CEO and  founder of Christmas land on a manual  typewriter no less that he would do  anything to get there  that's when Charlie recruits him as the  new chief of security since the old one  was killed by Charlie for botching the  kidnapping of Danny the young boy from  episode 1 Bing is the perfect loyal  henchman easy to manipulate and spurred  by childhood trauma being himself was  treated cruelly by his father so he  knows what it's like for a child to be  abused his father gave him a gas mask as  a Christmas present when he was a child  a hand-me-down from his days in Nam and  chemical attacks Bing would later go on  to use this mask when gassing his  victims gasps he acquired from his job  and it's fun to see being having evaded  the police at the end of the season now  known 